t and it may never have happened if  that doubt had grown roots the world  needs more fresh voices like Kristen's  it needs strong and different points of  view and  characters as fascinating as January it  can be a lonely room we live in as a  woman director or writer it's not  surprising we may need a little bit  extra encouragement it falls on all of  us to see and acknowledge those trying  to do those tasks those who need to have  proof that they can do it so Kristen  Rock maker we're here tonight to add to  your proof to say that you are very  talented writer and to welcome you up as  one of this year's Nichols fellows  [Applause]  okay thank you  Thanks I'll try not that they thank you  quite so much as I did in my my video  but thank you Jen that was um really  amazing you made me sound so good you  made me want to hang out with me haha  that's not easy to do you guys were so  good those scene has been in my head for  so long so to see it come to life is  just amazing and even better than I  could have imagined so thank you  I want to thank everybody who came out  I'm from New Jersey so some people were  local some people came from afar and it  really means so much to me to have the  support so thank you  and I thank my mom who has encouraged my  writing since I was a kid and who was  home in New Jersey with my children who  I am sure are stuffing their face with  Halloween candy since mom and dad aren't  there I want to thank my husband who has  supported me for many years in big ways  and small ways including making sure he  was home for Halloween the other day  while I was here and then hopping on a  plane the next morning to come out and  support me so thank you Morris I love  you and lastly I want to thank the  Academy it feels really nice to say that  but no I really do because I feel like  confidence is something that you really  need to succeed in this industry and I  feel like it's something that many women  struggle with including myself and even  w